# gitleaks fingerprint allowlist — INSTANCE-scoped, one line per triaged
# finding. Format: <commit>:<path>:<rule>:<line>
#
# Why this file exists alongside .gitleaks.toml: the toml allowlist is
# class-scoped (a path or regex exempts everything matching it, forever).
# Some findings are false positives as INSTANCES but their shape is exactly
# what a real secret looks like, so exempting the class would blind the
# scanner to the thing it exists to catch. Those go here, individually, with
# the reason written down.
#
# Rule for adding a line: name what the value actually is and why it grants
# nothing. "It's in a doc" is not a reason — the repo is public.

